-- Since top-level initialisation rule I2, `medaka check`, `run` and `build` refuse this
-- program with T-TOPLEVEL-EFFECT before any engine runs: `side` is a top-level value
-- whose initialiser performs <Stdout> (test/rejection_parity_fixtures.txt pins that on
-- native and wasm). The prelude-free llvm probe runs no typechecker, so it still emits
-- the program with `side` unreferenced and never run, and keeps the "ok" golden,
-- including when the prelude is linked as a separate object and source DCE is off.
main = putStrLn "ok"

side = putStrLn "BOOM"
